NUM-35: keep the aquifer upper-zone ET fraction within 0..1

The lower-zone ET rate is (1 - upperFrac) * MaxEvap times the depth fraction.
gwater_validateAquifer() rejected only ETu < 0, and getEvapRates() multiplies
ETu by the monthly pattern factor without a limit, so an effective fraction
above 1 made LowerEvap negative and added water to the saturated zone. Reject
ETu > 1 at input (as 6.0.0 already does) and cap the pattern-adjusted
fraction at 1. Upper-zone ET is unchanged, because it was already limited to
the available evaporation, which never exceeds MaxEvap.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-35_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/gwater.c b/src/legacy/engine/gwater.c
index d511143..0c159e2 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/gwater.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/gwater.c
@@ -353,6 +353,7 @@ void  gwater_validateAquifer(int aquiferIndex)
     ||   Aquifer[aquiferIndex].conductSlope      <  0.0
     ||   Aquifer[aquiferIndex].tensionSlope      <  0.0
     ||   Aquifer[aquiferIndex].upperEvapFrac     <  0.0
+    ||   Aquifer[aquiferIndex].upperEvapFrac     >  1.0
     ||   Aquifer[aquiferIndex].lowerEvapDepth    <  0.0
     ||   Aquifer[aquiferIndex].waterTableElev    <  Aquifer[aquiferIndex].bottomElev
     ||   Aquifer[aquiferIndex].upperMoisture     >  Aquifer[aquiferIndex].porosity 
@@ -747,6 +748,7 @@ void getEvapRates(double theta, double upperDepth)
         f = Pattern[p].factor[month-1];
     }
     upperFrac *= f;
+    upperFrac = MIN(upperFrac, 1.0);
 
     // --- upper zone evaporation requires that soil moisture
     //     be above the wilting point
